hat represents OOP in the past, in the present and nowadays."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe specific OOP features in the different timelines."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify OOP in history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare OOP in different timelines."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe OOP features past and present."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Mike</strong>: Hi, Lui. What are you doing? </br>\n<strong>Lui</strong>: I'm reading about the history of OOP. </br>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: What does it say?  </br>\n<strong>Lui</strong>: The author is telling that Object-Oriented Programming or OOP was the new conception of programming in the late 70's; it's a programming method that radically changed the way how programming worked. Its approach, based on the idea that we interact with single objects, it becomes part of a whole, so we cannot mix their attributes and capabilities. Therefore, each piece must have its own independent features."}, {"time": "40500", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Mike</strong>: So, was programing carried out differently in the past?  </br>\n<strong>Lui</strong>: Yes, The earliest approaches for programming consisted of an arrangement of variables and data to be included into an algorithm to fulfill the desired results. This was useful in simple programs, but as the complexity increased, it became more problematic to apply this method as any modification, required in its original definitions of data structured, could completely disturb the program running in other stages. Computer programmers tried to establish some programming rules to avoid side effects, but new ways to program were developing.  </br>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: What are examples of OOP programming languages?"}, {"time": "93000", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Lui</strong>: The first OOP language was Simula 67, created in the late 60's;  Smalltalk created in the 70's; finally, C++ arrived in the 80's. C++ is probably the most used programming language, and it holds all the features of an OOP language. Nowadays, languages such as Java and Visual Basic are becoming very popular in OOP languages.</br>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: What are the main features of OOP?</br>\n<strong>Lui</strong>: The main feature is the programming itself, because it is made with objects, and each object is independent. So, it has its own characteristics and procedures which indicate that it is an innovative way to integrate data."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le01ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": "01.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "02.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "03.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "04.jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what OOP is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give information about key features related to OOP."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk briefly about the history of OOP. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How did programming languages work in the past? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What object based languages do you know? What is your favorite? Why? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": 